slug: cohort-case-control-cross-sectional
title: Cohort, Case-Control and Cross-Sectional Studies
area: Research & Evidence
level: Clinical
best: Second year onwards
minutes: 14
hook: You cannot randomly assign people to smoke, to lift heavy loads or to get injured. For many questions in physiotherapy, observational studies are all we have. Learn to tell the three main types apart, and to ask the one question that matters: what else could explain this? || Aap logon ko random tareeqe se cigarette peene, bhaari wazan uthane ya zakhmi hone ke liye tay nahi kar sakte. Physiotherapy ke bohat se sawalon ke liye observational studies hi hamare paas hain. Teen bari qismon ko alag karna seekhein, aur woh ek sawal poochhna jo ahem hai: aur kya is ki wajah ho sakta hai?
goal: By the end, you'll tell cohort, case-control and cross-sectional studies apart, know which questions each can answer, understand confounding and reverse causation, and read an observational result with the right caution. || End tak aap cohort, case-control aur cross-sectional studies ko alag karenge, jaanenge har kis sawal ka jawab de sakta hai, confounding aur reverse causation samjhenge, aur observational nateeje ko sahi ehtiyat se parhenge.

say: In an **observational study**, researchers watch what happens and do not assign treatments. A **cohort study** follows a group over time from exposure to outcome. A **case-control study** starts with people who have an outcome (cases) and people who do not (controls), and looks back for exposures. A **cross-sectional study** takes a snapshot of everyone at one moment. They can show **association**, but proving cause needs extra care. || **Observational study** mein muhaqqiq dekhte hain kya hota hai aur ilaaj tay nahi karte. **Cohort study** ek group ko waqt ke saath exposure se outcome tak follow karti hai. **Case-control study** un logon (cases) se shuru hoti hai jin ka nateeja hua aur un se jin ka nahi hua (controls), aur peechay exposures dekhti hai. **Cross-sectional study** ek lamhe par sab ka snapshot leti hai. Yeh **association** dikha sakti hain, lekin wajah sabit karne ke liye mazeed ehtiyat chahiye.
analogy: Think of **detectives**. A cohort study is like following suspects for a year and noting who does what. A case-control study is like starting with the crime and looking back at who was around. A cross-sectional study is like one photograph of the whole street. Each tells you something, but none proves guilt alone. || **Jasooson** ko sochein. Cohort study aisi hai jaise shuk-zadgan ko saal bhar follow karna aur dekhna kaun kya karta hai. Case-control aisi hai jaise jurm se shuru kar ke peechay dekhna ke kaun mojood tha. Cross-sectional aisi hai jaise poori gali ki ek tasveer. Har ek kuch batati hai, lekin koi akeli mujrim sabit nahi karti.
compare: Three observational designs side by side || Teen observational designs saath saath
head: Design || Design ;; How it works || Kaise kaam karta hai ;; Best for || Behtareen kis liye
row: Cohort || Cohort ;; Follow exposed and unexposed people forward in time || Exposed aur ghair-exposed logon ko aage waqt mein follow karein ;; Prognosis, risk and how often an outcome happens; the time order is clear || Prognosis, khatra aur nateeje ki frequency; waqt ki tarteeb saaf
row: Case-control || Case-control ;; Start with cases and controls, look back for exposures || Cases aur controls se shuru, peechay exposures dekhein ;; Rare outcomes and quick answers, but memory and control choice can bias || Nadir nateeje aur tez jawab, lekin yaadasht aur control ka intikhab bias la sakte hain
row: Cross-sectional || Cross-sectional ;; Measure exposure and outcome at the same moment || Exposure aur outcome ek hi lamhe naapein ;; How common a problem is, and generating ideas, but cannot show which came first || Masla kitna aam hai, aur khayalat paida karna, lekin nahi dikha sakta pehle kya aaya
check: A researcher follows 500 office workers for two years and records who develops neck pain, comparing those with high versus low screen time. What design is this? || Ek muhaqqiq 500 daftari karkunon ko do saal follow karta hai aur dekhta hai kis ko gardan dard hota hai, zyada aur kam screen time walon ka muqabla karte hue. Yeh kaun sa design hai?
ok: A cohort study || Cohort study || Yes — a group is followed forward in time from exposure to outcome. || Haan — ek group ko exposure se outcome tak aage waqt mein follow kiya jata hai.
no: A case-control study || Case-control study || It would start from people who already have neck pain. || Yeh un logon se shuru hoti jinhein pehle se gardan dard hai.
no: A cross-sectional study || Cross-sectional study || It takes one snapshot, not a two-year follow-up. || Yeh ek snapshot leti hai, do saal ka follow-up nahi.
check: A survey finds that people with back pain sit longer each day than people without. A journalist writes "Sitting causes back pain". What is the best reply? || Survey paata hai ke peeth dard wale log bina dard walon se roz zyada baithte hain. Ek sahafi likhta hai "Baithna peeth dard paida karta hai". Behtareen jawab kya hai?
ok: This is cross-sectional, so we cannot tell which came first; people with pain might sit more because standing hurts, which is reverse causation || Yeh cross-sectional hai, isliye pata nahi pehle kya aaya; dard wale log is liye zyada baith sakte hain ke khade hona dukhta hai, yeh reverse causation hai || Yes — association is not cause, and the direction may run the other way. || Haan — association wajah nahi, aur rukh ulta bhi ho sakta hai.
no: The result proves sitting is harmful || Nateeja sabit karta hai ke baithna nuqsandeh hai || A snapshot cannot prove cause. || Snapshot wajah sabit nahi kar sakta.
no: Surveys are always wrong || Surveys hamesha ghalat hote hain || They are useful for what they can answer. || Woh jis ka jawab de sakte hain us ke liye mufeed hain.
check: A cohort study finds that people who exercise have less heart disease. Which factor could confound this? || Cohort study paata hai ke exercise karne walon ko dil ki bimari kam hai. Is ko kaun si wajah confound kar sakti hai?
ok: Exercisers may also smoke less, eat better and have higher income; these other factors might explain part of the difference || Exercise karne wale shayad cigarette kam peeyen, behtar khayen aur zyada kamayen; yeh doosri wajuhaat farq ke kuch hissay ki wazahat kar sakti hain || Yes — confounders are related to both the exposure and the outcome. || Haan — confounders exposure aur outcome dono se juday hote hain.
no: The study was too large || Study bohat bari thi || Size does not create confounding. || Size confounding paida nahi karti.
no: Heart disease causes people to exercise less, which is irrelevant || Dil ki bimari logon ko kam exercise karwati hai, jo ghair mutaliq hai || That is reverse causation, which is relevant. || Yeh reverse causation hai, jo mutaliq hai.
mistake: **Writing "causes" when the study only shows "is linked to".** Observational studies can suggest a cause, especially when the link is strong, consistent, comes in the right time order and shows a dose-response, but they rarely prove it. Use words that match the design: "is associated with", "was linked to", "may increase the risk". Also, check which factors were adjusted for, and which were not. || **"Wajah hai" likhna jab study sirf "juda hua hai" dikhati hai.** Observational studies wajah ka ishara de sakti hain, khaaskar jab talluq mazboot, mutasawi, sahi waqt ki tarteeb mein ho aur dose-response dikhaye, lekin shayad hi sabit karti hain. Design se milte alfaaz istemal karein: "se juda hai", "se link hua", "khatra barha sakta hai". Yeh bhi dekhein ke kin factors ko adjust kiya gaya aur kin ko nahi.
clinic: **Explain "linked to" honestly.** If a patient says "I read that sitting causes back pain", respond: "Studies show people who sit a lot often have more back pain, but it is not clear that sitting is the cause. Movement breaks and a gradual return to activity are good for most people anyway." This teaches patients that headlines are not the whole story. || **"Se juda hua hai" imaandari se samjhayein.** Agar mareez kahe "maine parha baithna peeth dard paida karta hai", jawab dein: "Studies dikhati hain jo log bohat baithte hain unhein aksar zyada peeth dard hota hai, lekin yeh wazeh nahi ke baithna wajah hai. Harkat ke waqfe aur sargarmi mein tadreeji wapsi zyada tar logon ke liye waise bhi achhi hai." Isse mareez seekhte hain ke sar-khat poori kahani nahi.
reveal: Why can a case-control study find a link to a rare disease with only a few hundred people? || Case-control study chand sau logon se nadir bimari ka talluq kaise dhoondh sakti hai? || Because it starts with the cases. In a cohort study, you would need to follow tens of thousands of people to see enough rare events. A case-control study collects the few people who already have the rare outcome and compares them with controls. The price is more risk of recall bias and of badly chosen controls. || Kyunke yeh cases se shuru hoti hai. Cohort study mein nadir waqiyaat kaafi dekhne ke liye dahion hazar logon ko follow karna parta. Case-control study un chand logon ko jama karti hai jinhein pehle se nadir nateeja hai aur unka controls se muqabla karti hai. Qeemat yeh hai ke recall bias aur ghalat chune gaye controls ka khatra zyada hota hai.
case: A cohort study finds that runners who warm up for at least 10 minutes have 40 percent fewer injuries than those who do not. The authors recommend all runners warm up. || The warm-up groups may differ in other ways: more experienced runners, better shoes, more sleep. These confounders may explain part of the difference. || Check whether the study adjusted for experience, training load and shoes. If so, say the link is more convincing; if not, say a trial is needed to be sure. || A reasonable plan: recommend warming up because it is low-risk, but be honest that the evidence does not prove it prevents injury.
safety: **A link is not enough to change safe care.** If an observational study suggests a risk, such as a medicine or technique linked to a rare harm, take it seriously and check other sources. For a harm signal, do not wait for a trial: reduce exposure while you look, especially for frail patients. || **Ek talluq safe care badalne ke liye kaafi nahi.** Agar observational study kisi khatre ka ishara kare, jaise dawai ya technique jo nadir nuqsan se juda ho, to isay seriyas lein aur doosre zarai dekhein. Nuqsan ke ishare par trial ka intezar na karein: dhoondte waqt exposure kam karein, khaaskar kamzor mareezon ke liye.
evidence: Grimes and Schulz described cohort studies as following groups forward from exposure to outcome, which gives clear time order and lets researchers measure the incidence of outcomes, while noting the problems of loss to follow-up, long durations and confounding. Schulz and Grimes described case-control studies as research in reverse, efficient for rare diseases and quick to complete but vulnerable to recall bias and to bias in selecting controls. || Grimes aur Schulz ne cohort studies ko aise bayan kiya ke woh groups ko exposure se outcome tak aage follow karti hain, jo waqt ki saaf tarteeb deta hai aur muhaqqiqon ko nateejon ki incidence naapne deta hai, jabke follow-up se nikalne, lambi muddat aur confounding ke masail bhi bataye. Schulz aur Grimes ne case-control studies ko ulti research kaha, jo nadir bimariyon ke liye mu'assir aur jaldi mukammal hone wali hain lekin recall bias aur controls chunne ke bias ke liye kamzor hain.
memory: **Cohort forward, Case-control backward, Cross-sectional snapshot.** And always ask: what else could explain this? || **Cohort aage, Case-control peechay, Cross-sectional snapshot.** Aur hamesha poochhein: aur kya is ki wajah ho sakta hai?
summary: Cohort studies follow people forward, case-control studies look back from cases, and cross-sectional studies take a snapshot. || Cohort studies logon ko aage follow karti hain, case-control cases se peechay dekhti hain, aur cross-sectional snapshot leti hain.
summary: Observational studies show association; confounding and reverse causation can mislead. || Observational studies association dikhati hain; confounding aur reverse causation gumrah kar sakte hain.
summary: Use words that match the design, and check what was adjusted for. || Design se milte alfaaz istemal karein, aur dekhein kin factors ko adjust kiya gaya.
card: Which design starts with people who already have the outcome? || Kaun sa design un logon se shuru hota hai jinhein pehle se nateeja hai? || Case-control. || Case-control.
card: What is confounding? || Confounding kya hai? || A third factor related to both exposure and outcome that distorts the link. || Teesri wajah jo exposure aur outcome dono se judi ho aur talluq bigaad de.
card: What is reverse causation? || Reverse causation kya hai? || The outcome causes the exposure, not the other way round. || Nateeja exposure ki wajah hai, ulta nahi.
card: Which design best shows time order and incidence? || Waqt ki tarteeb aur incidence kaun sa design behtar dikhata hai? || A cohort study. || Cohort study.
deeper: The hierarchy of evidence || /learn/hierarchy-of-evidence-and-where-it-misleads || Where observational designs sit. || Observational designs kahan aate hain.
deeper: Why treatments seem to work || /learn/why-treatments-seem-to-work || Confounding in plain language. || Confounding saade alfaaz mein.
source: Grimes DA, Schulz KF. Cohort studies: marching towards outcomes. Lancet 2002;359:341-345. || Cohort studies marching towards outcomes Grimes Schulz
source: Schulz KF, Grimes DA. Case-control studies: research in reverse. Lancet 2002;359:431-434. || Case-control studies research in reverse Schulz Grimes
